<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Finding trigonometric ratios of negative angles using the unit circle</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Let \(P\) be the point where the terminal side of the angle \(\theta = {@theta@}\) meets the unit circle. Give exact values.</p>
<p>(a) The coordinates of \(P\): \(\Big(\) [[input:ansx]] \(,\) [[input:ansy]] \(\Big)\) [[validation:ansx]] [[validation:ansy]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>
<p>(b) \(\sin(\theta)=\) [[input:ans_sin]] [[validation:ans_sin]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>
<p>(c) \(\cos(\theta)=\) [[input:ans_cos]] [[validation:ans_cos]] [[feedback:prt3]]</p>
<p>(d) \(\tan(\theta)=\) [[input:ans_tan]] [[validation:ans_tan]] [[feedback:prt4]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A negative angle is measured clockwise from the positive \(x\)-axis. The point on the unit circle at angle \(\theta\) is \(P=(\cos\theta,\,\sin\theta)\).</p>
<p>(a) \(P=\left({@x_coord@},\,{@y_coord@}\right)\).</p>
<p>(b) \(\sin\theta\) is the \(y\)-coordinate of \(P\): \(\sin({@theta@})={@sin_theta@}\).</p>
<p>(c) \(\cos\theta\) is the \(x\)-coordinate of \(P\): \(\cos({@theta@})={@cos_theta@}\).</p>
<p>(d) \(\tan\theta=\dfrac{\sin\theta}{\cos\theta}=\dfrac{ {@sin_theta@} }{ {@cos_theta@} }={@tan_theta@}\).</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
